1
00:00:00,886 --> 00:00:02,856
(Howard(entering):)All right, we got a problem.

2
00:00:02,855 --> 00:00:03,675
(Leonard:)What's up?

3
00:00:03,699 --> 00:00:06,259
(Howard:)The Air Force contacted me
about our quantum gyroscope.

4
00:00:06,354 --> 00:00:07,184
(Howard:)They want to have
a meeting.

5
00:00:07,208 --> 00:00:07,788
(Leonard:)Really?

6
00:00:07,793 --> 00:00:09,923
(Raj:)Yeah. This military guy
showed up at Howard's door.

7
00:00:09,928 --> 00:00:11,428
(Raj:)He was terrifying.

8
00:00:11,430 --> 00:00:12,760
(Sheldon:)Oh, what did he say?

9
00:00:12,765 --> 00:00:14,035
(Raj:)He gave me his business card

10
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:18,033
(Raj:)and asked me to please
pass it along to Howard.

11
00:00:18,037 --> 00:00:20,467
(Sheldon:)That doesn't sound terrifying.

12
00:00:20,472 --> 00:00:23,002
(Raj:)To a white guy born here, no.

13
00:00:24,910 --> 00:00:26,740
(Raj:)If you are a brown guy
whose name has

14
00:00:26,745 --> 00:00:29,715
(Raj:)a lot of syllables in it--
terrifying.

15
00:00:30,453 --> 00:00:33,083
(Leonard:)You realize if the military declares our
research classified,

16
00:00:33,089 --> 00:00:35,419
(Leonard:)they can take the whole
thing away from us.

17
00:00:35,424 --> 00:00:36,754
(Howard:)And if that happens,

18
00:00:36,759 --> 00:00:38,189
(Howard:)we'll never be able
to sell it commercially.

19
00:00:38,194 --> 00:00:39,464
(Leonard:)There goes our big payday.
I was counting

20
00:00:39,462 --> 00:00:41,832
(Howard:)on that money-- I need
to make as much as my wife

21
00:00:41,831 --> 00:00:44,431
(Howard:)so I don't have
to try so hard in bed.

22
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:46,133
(Leonard:)You do that, too?

23
00:00:46,135 --> 00:00:49,005
(Howard:)Oh, yeah. How do you think
I stay this thin?

24
00:00:49,005 --> 00:00:52,175
(Sheldon:)Gentlemen, I think we are
losing sight of the real issue.

25
00:00:52,175 --> 00:00:55,305
(Sheldon:)We are on the precipice
of becoming faceless cogs

26
00:00:55,311 --> 00:00:57,641
(Sheldon:)in the military-industrial
complex.

27
00:00:57,647 --> 00:01:00,347
(Sheldon:)Isn't that exciting?

28
00:01:00,349 --> 00:01:01,679
(Raj:)You're kidding, right?

29
00:01:01,684 --> 00:01:04,654
Not at all. In Star Wars,
when the stormtroopers

30
00:01:04,654 --> 00:01:06,754
(Sheldon:)would march
in perfect formation,

31
00:01:06,756 --> 00:01:09,056
(Sheldon:)harassing civilians,
didn't you ever think,

32
00:01:09,058 --> 00:01:11,228
"Hey, that could be me"?

33
00:01:11,227 --> 00:01:12,897
(Howard:)Sheldon,
we could be contributing

34
00:01:12,895 --> 00:01:15,525
(Howard:)to a weapons system
that oppresses mankind

35
00:01:15,531 --> 00:01:18,131
(Howard:)for the next thousand years.

36
00:01:18,134 --> 00:01:20,434
(Sheldon:)Okay, Howard's on board.
What do you think, Leonard?

37
00:01:21,504 --> 00:01:25,104
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

